※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4933 LANG_MARK_NOT_NEEDED

※ What a callee is asked is what it does, not what it says.  `even` and `odd`
※ call only each other, and each is marked `@[impure]` because the other is --
※ which justifies nothing: neither changes anything, so both are reported, in
※ one build rather than one at a time.  `counted` writes a variable at the top
※ level, so its mark and that of `tally`, which calls it, are needed.

let std := ⎕import("std")

let calls: mut u8 = 0u8

@[impure]
fn counted():
    calls ← calls + 1u8

@[impure]
fn tally():
    counted()

@[impure]
fn even(n: u8) → bool:
    if n = 0u8: true else: odd(n - 1u8)

@[impure]
fn odd(n: u8) → bool:
    if n = 0u8: false else: even(n - 1u8)

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    tally()
    if even(4u8) ∧ calls = 1u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
